  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO AITripPlannerLLMAgent errors; the blocker pre-exists this change):
    Both builds fail at the SAME single error, in a PRE-EXISTING file that this surface does not touch:
        TeslaSync/feature-views/AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift:18:8: error: unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'
    Root cause is the documented parallel-merge structural issue: co-located "*.Tests.swift" files are compiled into the
    APP target (project.yml includes the whole feature-views/shared-surfaces directories as app sources), and the app
    target cannot resolve XCTest. The Swift driver fails fast on that module-resolution error, so it never reaches the
    second documented blocker (`public struct DashboardWidgetSize` redefined 15× across dashboard-widgets → "ambiguous
    for type lookup") nor macOS development-signing. grep of both build logs for a shared-surfaces / AITripPlannerLLMAgent
    "error:" = 0 hits; the only error source file is the pre-existing AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift.
    This surface follows the sanctioned feature-views convention (its predecessor AIRestorePanel co-locates *.Tests.swift
    the same way, and the prompt's allowed-files glob is AITripPlannerLLMAgent.*), so its own tests share that pattern —
    but they are CORRECT and PASS in a proper test target (the isolated SwiftPM test target above: 46/46). Excluding
    *.Tests.swift from the app target (or compiling them in the test target) is a project-wide config change owned by the
    P4/P99 Apple acceptance gate, NOT a single surface prompt (task rule: do not fix pre-existing unrelated breakage).
    This is exactly what apps/macos-pending-verifications.md defers to the ADR-012 macos-latest CI runner; a pending-
    verification row is recorded there.

